{%- comment -%}
  Shared markup for the `comparison-row` atom (type `ComparisonRow`; renders as
  the <dm-comparison-table-row> custom element) — the single source of truth for
  what this atom renders. Two callers, and they must not drift:
    - blocks/dm-comparison-row.liquid — as a Shopify theme block (shallow)
    - the inline emitter              — as {% render %} inside a parent's
                                        dm_inline setting past depth 8

  Params are flat (Liquid has no object literal). Slot content (the label cell +
  one value cell per product column, in order) arrives PRE-RENDERED as the
  `children` string. A `composition` atom — it carries no universal
  customStyles / margin / hideOn, only its own `kind`.

  The row uses subgrid (declared in dm-theme.css) so its cells inherit the
  table's column tracks; `data-comparison-row-kind` bands its typography.
{%- endcomment -%}
<dm-comparison-table-row
  data-atom-type="comparison-table-row"
  {% if kind != blank %}data-comparison-row-kind="{{ kind }}"{% endif %}
  {{ shopify_attributes }}
>
  {{ children }}
</dm-comparison-table-row>
